-- title:
--   A Frobenius functional on the complex weight-2 Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number, let $S_2 =$ `CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 M) 2` be the space of weight-$2$ cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(M)$, and let $\mathbb{T}_{\mathbb{Z}} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) be the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2)$ generated by the set of operators consisting of `heckeTLin` for every prime $\ell$ not dividing $M$ together with `heckeULin` for every prime $q$ dividing $M$ (the excluded set of primes being empty here). Write $\mathbb{T}_{\mathbb{C}} =$ `Algebra.adjoin ℂ` of the underlying set of $\mathbb{T}_{\mathbb{Z}}$, the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2)$ generated by all these Hecke operators. The assertion is that there exists a $\mathbb{C}$-linear map $l : \mathbb{T}_{\mathbb{C}} \to \mathbb{C}$ such that for every $a \in \mathbb{T}_{\mathbb{C}}$, if $l(ab) = 0$ for all $b \in \mathbb{T}_{\mathbb{C}}$, then $a = 0$; that is, the bilinear pairing $(a,b) \mapsto l(ab)$ on $\mathbb{T}_{\mathbb{C}}$ has zero left kernel. Only this one-sided non-degeneracy is asserted; no symmetry, perfectness, or reducedness of $\mathbb{T}_{\mathbb{C}}$ is claimed.
--
--   This is the forms-side reading of the Gorenstein property of the weight-$2$ Hecke algebra of $\Gamma_0(M)$ over a field of characteristic zero: existence of a linear form whose associated pairing is left non-degenerate reflects that $S_2(\Gamma_0(M),\mathbb{C})$ is cyclic over $\mathbb{T}_{\mathbb{C}}$. It is used in the construction of two-dimensional bases of parabolic homomorphisms and the computation of the dimension of a Hecke eigenspace.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_heckeAlgebra_adjoin_exists_frobenius_form.lean

import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem CuspForm.heckeAlgebra_adjoin_exists_frobenius_form (M : ℕ) [NeZero M] :
    ∃ l : (Algebra.adjoin ℂ
        ((CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 ∅ : Set
          (Module.End ℂ (CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 M) 2))))) →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ,
      ∀ a, (∀ b, l (a * b) = 0) → a = 0 := by sorry
